@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>.
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>.
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/>.
@prefix fract: <https://fractiverse.com/ns#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix : <https://fractiverse.com/map/ontology-full#>.

# The Fractiverse Full Ontology, v3
#
# Changes from v2, each explained on the node it affects:
#   * Duality inserted between the Fractiverse and the Motion/Stillness pair. OPTIONAL:
#     naming the pair of original dualities instead is a defensible choice, and this node
#     can be deleted without touching anything else.
#   * Stillness left childless, which is correct and deliberate — see its page. An earlier
#     revision moved Structure under it, which was a misreading and is undone.
#   * Axiom IV and Candidate Axiom 3 connected to C4, completing the pairing.
#   * fract:containedIn added everywhere, so the containing parent is stated rather
#     than inferred from document order.
#   * Tier numbers omitted. They are recomputed as 1 + max(all parents), so stating
#     them can only disagree with the edges — as one did in v2.
#   * fract:onAxis on the two ends of the axis.
#   * fract:resetsTo from Stillness back to the Fractiverse, closing the cycle Axiom II
#     describes. That edge bears no tier and is exempt from the acyclic rule, which is how
#     a hierarchy can state a loop without collapsing.
#   * schema:text used for the page behind each node, where there is something to say.

<https://fractiverse.com/map/ontology-full> a skos:ConceptScheme;
    dcterms:title "The Fractiverse Full Ontology";
    skos:hasTopConcept :fractiverse.

# --- The unknowable container ----------------------------------------------

:fractiverse a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "The Fractiverse";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-root";
    fract:onAxis true;
    dcterms:description "The ultimate unknowable container.";
    schema:text """# The Fractiverse

The ultimate container. Unknowable in the sense the Gnostics meant by the Monad:
not hidden, but prior to the distinctions that knowing requires.

Everything below is a distinction made within it. It sits on the axis because it is
the one thing that is not yet differentiated from anything.""";
    skos:topConceptOf <https://fractiverse.com/map/ontology-full>.

# --- The first distinction -------------------------------------------------
#
# Restored. v2 had Motion and Stillness hanging directly off the Fractiverse, which
# skips the step that makes them a pair rather than two arbitrary children.

:duality a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Duality";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "The first distinction: that there is more than one thing.";
    schema:text """# Duality

The first cut. Not "two things" but the possibility of two — the appearance of
difference within what was undifferentiated.

Everything below is a consequence of this one move, which is why it is the only child
of the Fractiverse.""";
    skos:broader :fractiverse;
    fract:containedIn :fractiverse.

:motion a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Motion";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "The changing pole of the first duality. Everything emerges from here.";
    schema:text """# Motion

The split of Duality from the singularity is the catalyst — the Big Bang — and motion
begot more motion. Every branch of this ontology descends from here, which is not an
imbalance to be corrected but the claim itself: there is nothing in the observable
universe without motion.

Its twin, Stillness, is childless for the same reason.""";
    skos:broader :duality;
    fract:containedIn :duality.

:stillness a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Stillness";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    fract:terminal true;
    dcterms:description "Terminal entropy. Heat death. Deliberately childless.";
    schema:text """# Stillness

**Childless on purpose.** Not an unfinished branch.

Stillness is the final end state of entropy — heat death. Everything in the observable
universe, and in the quantum, has motion; part of why absolute zero is unreachable is
that there is no state of the universe in which nothing moves. So nothing *emerges from*
Stillness. It is where things arrive, not where things come from.

An earlier revision of this file moved Structure under here, reading Axiom II's
"field-induced **ordering** (Structure)" as the still pole. That was a misreading: the
ordering half of Axiom II's cycle is something motion *does*, and terminal entropy is
its opposite, not its home. Structure belongs under Motion.

## The cycle

Axiom II says persistence comes from "a recurrent cycle" and that "Death (Key 13) is not
an end, but the mandatory refresh rate of the information field." So Stillness is not
where the story stops — it is where it turns over.

That is a **loop**, and a hierarchy cannot hold one: tiers are 1 + max(parents), which
requires an acyclic graph. The `fract:resetsTo` edge below is the resolution. It is drawn,
it is exported, and it is deliberately excluded from the tier computation and from the
cycle check — so it states "this returns to that" without claiming either derives from the
other. It is the one relation in this format allowed to be circular, because the framework
it serves is.""";
    skos:broader :duality;
    fract:containedIn :duality;
    fract:resetsTo :fractiverse.

# --- The three quantities --------------------------------------------------
#
# qs, qp, qc read as a triad, and Axiom I says why: the temporal interval is composed
# of three orthogonal dimensions. They are kept as siblings-in-kind across the duality
# rather than being bundled under one pole.

:structure a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Structure (qs)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "The ordering quantity. Axiom II's structure-forming half — something motion does.";
    skos:broader :motion;
    fract:containedIn :motion.

:dynamics a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Dynamics";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "The dissociating half: change, reset, flow.";
    skos:broader :motion;
    fract:containedIn :motion.

:phase a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Phase (qp)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Where in a cycle. Axiom I's interaction scale, t2.";
    skos:broader :dynamics;
    fract:containedIn :dynamics.

:scale a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Scale (qc)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "At what magnitude. Axiom I's cosmological scale, t3.";
    skos:broader :dynamics;
    fract:containedIn :dynamics.

# --- The eight axioms ------------------------------------------------------
#
# Each draws on the quantities it actually concerns. The containing parent is stated,
# so the convergence is unambiguous rather than resolved by whichever edge came first
# in the file.

:principia-axiom-I a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Principia Axiom I: 3D Time";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Time is three orthogonal dimensions; masses are its eigenvalues.";
    skos:broader :phase, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :phase.

:candidate-axiom-3 a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Candidate Axiom 3: Universal Scaling";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Critical transitions collapse onto a universal curve.";
    skos:broader :phase, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :phase.

:principia-axiom-II a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Principia Axiom II: Thermodynamic Pulse";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Persistence through a cycle of ordering and reset.";
    skos:broader :structure, :phase;
    fract:containedIn :structure.

:candidate-axiom-4 a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Candidate Axiom 4: Resonant Phase-Locking";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Coupled oscillators lock phase above a critical coupling.";
    skos:broader :structure, :phase;
    fract:containedIn :phase.

:principia-axiom-III a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Principia Axiom III: Scale-Invariant Coupling";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "t2 acts as a universal scale-coupler; everything is a fractal hologram.";
    skos:broader :structure, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :scale.

:candidate-axiom-1 a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Candidate Axiom 1: Geometry Constrains Observables";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Amplituhedron: locality and unitarity emerge from positivity.";
    skos:broader :structure, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :structure.

:principia-axiom-IV a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Principia Axiom IV: Crystallization Spectrum";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Potential becomes real through four stages, C1 to C4.";
    schema:text """# Axiom IV: The Crystallization Spectrum

This is the axiom that *states* the C1 to C4 spectrum, and in v2 nothing flowed out of
it — the axiom defining the ladder was not attached to the ladder.

It now feeds C4 directly, which is what the pairing pattern predicts: six axioms pair
into C1, C2 and C3, leaving Axiom IV and Candidate Axiom 3 as the remaining pair. The
axiom about the spectrum itself and the axiom about universal critical transitions are
exactly the two that belong at the meta stage.""";
    skos:broader :structure, :phase, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :structure.

:candidate-axiom-2 a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Candidate Axiom 2: Topological Protection";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Topological invariants cannot degrade continuously, enabling cross-scale coherence.";
    skos:broader :structure, :phase, :scale;
    fract:containedIn :structure.

# --- The crystallization stages -------------------------------------------

:c1-lattice a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "C1: Lattice Crystallization";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Physical stability. The Emperor.";
    skos:broader :principia-axiom-II, :candidate-axiom-1;
    fract:containedIn :principia-axiom-II.

:c2-dynamic a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "C2: Dynamic Crystallization";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Isolated potential. The Hermit.";
    skos:broader :principia-axiom-I, :candidate-axiom-4;
    fract:containedIn :principia-axiom-I.

:c3-informational a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "C3: Informational Crystallization";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "Directed attention. The Magician.";
    skos:broader :principia-axiom-III, :candidate-axiom-2;
    fract:containedIn :principia-axiom-III.

# --- The four operators ---------------------------------------------------

:resonance a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Resonance (R)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "How strongly components couple.";
    skos:broader :c2-dynamic;
    fract:containedIn :c2-dynamic.

:emergent-complexity a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Emergent Complexity (Sigma)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "What the coupling produces that the parts do not have.";
    skos:broader :c3-informational;
    fract:containedIn :c3-informational.

:temporal-stability a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Temporal Stability (Gamma)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "How long a pattern persists across the reset cycle.";
    skos:broader :c1-lattice, :c2-dynamic;
    fract:containedIn :c1-lattice.

:inter-scale-coupling a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Inter-Scale Coupling (Omega)";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "How a pattern at one scale reaches another.";
    skos:broader :c1-lattice, :c3-informational;
    fract:containedIn :c1-lattice.

# --- Where it all comes back together -------------------------------------

:consciousness a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "C4: Meta-Crystallization / Consciousness";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    fract:onAxis true;
    dcterms:description "Unified realization. The Sun.";
    schema:text """# C4: Meta-Crystallization

Where the four operators and the two remaining axioms reunify.

On the axis, declared rather than derived. The axis runs from the Fractiverse at the
apex to here at the base: the undifferentiated container and its full realization, the
two points that are not partial. Everything between them sits off the axis in
proportion to how much it has been differentiated and how little has yet flowed back
together.

That is Axiom IV drawn as a distance. C1, physical stability, sits at the rim; C4 sits
on the line.""";
    skos:broader :resonance, :emergent-complexity, :temporal-stability, :inter-scale-coupling,
                 :principia-axiom-IV, :candidate-axiom-3;
    fract:containedIn :resonance.

# --- A consequence, not an input ------------------------------------------
#
# Kept as a leaf on purpose. QFT is something the framework should account for rather
# than something that flows into consciousness, and its v2 tier of 7 disagreed with its
# own single edge — the importer computed 6.

:quantum-field-theory a skos:Concept;
    skos:prefLabel "Quantum Field Theory";
    fract:nodeType "spiral-node";
    dcterms:description "An account the framework has to be consistent with.";
    skos:broader :c3-informational;
    fract:containedIn :c3-informational.
